{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.648,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Working with Fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "Let us look at this red square. The area of the triangle inside it (coloured yellow) is half the area of the red square. So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.137,
            0.689,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "the area of the yellow triangle $= { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 8 } }$ square units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.176,
            0.625,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": "What fraction of this yellow triangle is shaded?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.2,
            0.691,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "The shaded region occupies $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ of the area of the yellow triangle. Are you able to see why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.693,
            0.167,
            0.848,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.263,
            0.639,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "The area of shaded part $\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{3}{32}$ square units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.305,
            0.828,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the shaded region occupies $\\frac { 3 } { 3 2 }$ of the area of the whole square."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.352,
            0.846,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "？ In each of the figures given below, find the fraction of the big square that the shaded region occupies."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.243,
            0.408,
            0.461,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.533,
            0.407,
            0.75,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.586,
            0.846,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "We will solve more interesting problems of this kind in a later chapter."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.643,
            0.449,
            0.664
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A Dramma-tic Donation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.673,
            0.846,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": "The following problem is translated from Bhāskarāchārya’s (Bhāskara II’s) book, Līlāvatī, written in 1150 CE."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.713,
            0.848,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": "“O wise one! A miser gave to a beggar $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ of $\\frac { 1 } { 1 6 }$ of $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ of $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ of $\\frac{2}{3}$ of $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ of a dramma. If you know the mathematics of fractions well, tell me O child, how many cowrie shells were given by the miser to the beggar.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.807,
            0.848,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "Dramma refers to a silver coin used in those times. The tale says that 1 dramma was equivalent to 1280 cowrie shells. Let’s see what fraction of a dramma the person gave:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.293,
            0.872,
            0.704,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": "$\\left( { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } \\times { \\frac { 3 } { 4 } } \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 1 6 } } \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } \\right) ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ part of a dramma."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.806,
            0.937,
            0.848,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "193"
        }
      ]
    }
